<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH BANK CSOB FIRST QUARTER GROSS PROFIT FALLS.</title>
<headline>CZECH BANK CSOB FIRST QUARTER GROSS PROFIT FALLS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for three month period</p>
<p>ending March 31, 1997, calculated according to Czech accounting</p>
<p>standards (in millions of crowns):</p>
<p> Gross profit			577.36   vs	 937.90</p>
<p> Interest income		 5,759.00   vs     4,175.73</p>
<p>Income from fees</p>
<p> and commissions		   382.67   vs	 394.77</p>
<p>Creation of reserves</p>
<p> to loans			  1,235.84   vs	 752.13</p>
<p>application of reserves</p>
<p> to loans			    957.61   vs	 380.71</p>
<p> Balance sheet total	 232,154.35   vs   210,604.02</p>
<p> Basic capital		   5,105.00   vs     5,105.00</p>
<p>NOTE. Full company name is Ceskoslovenska Obchodni Banka</p>
<p>a.s. (CSOB). CSOB, which is the country's fourth largest bank,</p>
<p>is controlled by the Czech National Bank, National Bank of</p>
<p>Slovakia, and Czech government agencies. Results were provided</p>
<p>by the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
